T4 CI matrix round 5 (FINAL) — windows never-torn transient contention
(gh run 42165202791). 2026-11-06.

== Mechanism (now complete, both error lines in evidence) ==

  workspace_test.go:280 write A: rename .tmp -> driver.lua: Access is denied
  workspace_test.go:269 reader: open driver.lua: Access is denied

Windows facts this run pinned down: FILE_SHARE_DELETE (round 4's
readers) permits DeleteFile but NOT MoveFileEx-replace-over — the
writer's rename still collides with any OPEN reader (writer sees
errno 5/32; replaceFile already retries). Symmetrically, opening the
target DURING an in-flight rename transiently returns
ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED to the reader. Both directions are transient
contention; round 4 fixed only the writer side, so the reader side
(erred out fatally at line 269) and the ~99%-duty reader loop (no
rename window ever opens) both still bit.

== Fix (three pieces, per brief) ==

1. internal/mcp/readshared_windows.go: readFileShared gains a bounded
   retry on errno 5/32 (200 x 10ms ~ 2s, mirroring replaceFile; the
   errno consts reused from rename_windows.go). Non-transient errors
   return immediately; ENOENT mapping unchanged. readFileSharedOnce
   split out as the single-attempt body.
2. workspace_test.go TestWriteDurableFileNeverTorn: 2ms inter-read
   gap in the reader loop — a real reader never zero-gap loops, and
   the replace needs an instant with the target unopened even against
   share-delete readers. Torn/absent-or-complete assertions unchanged;
   readers keep readFileShared (round 4).
3. Writer scanner (replaceFile) unchanged — already retries 5/32.

